> Compare exact Bernoulli means with observed frequencies

These1000 pulls per arm are an additional seeded diagnostic on probabilities.1,.4,.8. The original Gaussian/contextual tests and regret loops above retain their full source draw budgets.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/bandits_means.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){namespace e=dm::rl::environments;auto env=e::MultiArmedBandit::Bernoulli({.1f,.4f,.8f});env.reset(1);std::vector<double>x,mean,observed;for(int arm=0;arm<3;++arm){double sum=0;for(int i=0;i<1000;++i){env.reset();sum+=env.step(arm).reward;}x.push_back(arm);mean.push_back(env.mean(arm));observed.push_back(sum/1000);}dm::nn::save_npz("build/bandits_means.npz",{{"arm",dm::nn::from_vector(x)},{"mean",dm::nn::from_vector(mean)},{"observed",dm::nn::from_vector(observed)}});dm::graphics::RPlot::create().points(x,mean,"exact mean",{37,99,235},7).points(x,observed,"observed frequency",{234,88,12},5).x_label("Arm").y_label("Reward mean").title("Bernoulli reward expectations and1000 observed pulls").size(1000,550).save_svg("build/bandits_means.svg");}
```
